A1. A shingle belle. ~ FLAPPER
A6. These are all to the mustard. ~ HOTDOGS
A12. Something to look up to. ~ MOON
A14. Out of the presence of. ~ FROM
A15. A heavenly body. (Not made by Fisher.) ~ ORB
A17. A young rambler rose. ~ BUD
A19. Period of time. ~ ERA
A21. This will come out all right in the end. ~ TOE
A22. Things that husbands are always trained to carry. ~ PARCELS
A23. The wages of this is debt. ~ GIN
A24. A 1926 drinking bout. ~ PARTY
A26. To piece out. ~ EKE
A27. What subway riders do. ~ STAND
A29. The morning after the night before. ~ AM
A30. Bound by oath. ~ SWORN
A32. The "cracker" State (abbr.). ~ GA
A33. Your neighbor's child. ~ BRAT
A35. The first word in accidents. ~ OUCH
A38. One of the seasons. ~ PEPPER
A39. An ancestor. ~ MONKEY
A41. This is a head in France. ~ TETE
A43. Large stove used for drying. ~ KILN
A45. Part of the verb "to be." ~ AM
A47. Plaits. ~ PLATS
A50. A note of the scale. ~ FA
A51. African persuader. ~ RAZOR
A54. Topsy's girl friend. ~ EVA
A55. A sacred song. ~ PSALM
A57. Attempt. ~ TRY
A58. An admiral of the Swiss Navy. ~ OFFICER
A59. This makes that "fool girl complexion." ~ DAB
A60. A shade tree. ~ ELM
A61. Trinitrotoluene. (People go all to pieces over this.) ~ TNT
A62. A wise bird. ~ OWL
A63. A small quantity in Greece. ~ IOTA
A66. A fruit. ~ PEAR
A68. Poor fish. ~ SUCKERS
A69. The skins of these make excellent slippers. ~ BANANAS

D1. An important Chicagoan. ~ FOOTPAD
D2. The color of an imitation amber bead. ~ AMBER
D3. Italy's crossword river. ~ PO
D4. The favorite flower of the Chinese. ~ POPPY
D5. Half an em. ~ EN
D7. Preposition. ~ OF
D8. A support. ~ TRUSS
D9. Perform. ~ DO
D10. The last letter of the Greek alphabet. ~ OMEGA
D11. What every woman knows. ~ SCANDAL
D13. Nobody home. ~ CUCKOO
D16. When in Rome, do this. ~ ROAM
D17. Homework. ~ BREW
D18. A gentle animal. ~ DEER
D20. Something often found in a bathtub. ~ RING
D25. A submarine's ultimatum. ~ TORPEDO
D28. Something a red mustache does. ~ TICKLES
D30. The cost of living. ~ STEEP
D31. Sparking places. ~ NOOKS
D33. Wager. ~ BET
D34. Dexterous. ~ APT
D36. Prefix meaning "one." ~ UNI
D37. What an old hen usually is. ~ HEN
D40. Hold-ups. (Stop us if you've heard this before.) ~ GARTERS
D42. Something lifeguards are always doing in the summer. ~ SAVING
D44. Takes a chance on getting married. ~ CAMBLES
D46. Rich earth. ~ MARL
D48. This is never right. ~ LEFT
D49. Something the perfect husband would have to have. ~ TACT
D50. A weak spot in a pretzel. ~ FLAW
D52. Relating to or produced by fermentation. ~ ZYMIC
D53. A course of travel. ~ ROUTE
D55. What birds of fine feathers do. ~ PREEN
D56. Doll up. ~ ADORN
D64. All right (abbr.). ~ OK
D65. Anemic Radishes (init.). ~ AR
D66. The family goat. ~ PA
D67. Amateur Artichokes (init.). ~ AA


